# Single development server

Always use **ONE** Next.js / pnpm development server for this repo at `http://localhost:3000`. Never print `.env` secrets.

## Ownership

One dedicated **dev server** agent owns start and restart. That agent is the **only** process allowed to:

- Start/restart `pnpm dev` / `next dev`, kill the listener on port 3000, or restart the server in place
- Run `npx prisma generate` / `prisma generate` (the query engine DLL is locked by Next on Windows)
- Run any other command that replaces locked binaries Next is using — e.g. `pnpm add next`, overwriting `node_modules/next`, replacing `generated/prisma/query_engine-windows.dll.node`
- Use side-generate-and-copy workarounds for EPERM on the query engine

All other agents **MUST NOT**:

- Run `pnpm dev`, `next dev`, or any equivalent start command
- Kill, taskkill, or otherwise stop the process on port 3000
- Spawn a second server on 3001, 3002, or any other port
- Run `prisma generate` / `npx prisma generate`
- Work around EPERM by generating to `prisma-tmp` (or similar) and copying over the live client
- Bump `lib/db.ts` Prisma singleton keys as a generate workaround
- `pnpm add` / install packages that fail with EPERM because Next locks `node_modules/next` — if an install truly requires it, ask the server agent to stop, then install, then start again

If the server is dead, stale, or needs a Prisma/client refresh: tell the coordinator or the dedicated **dev server** agent. Do not restart it yourself.

## Prisma client after a migration

When another agent needs a new Prisma client after a migration:

1. They MAY run `npx prisma migrate deploy` (does not lock the engine the same way) if that is safe
2. They MUST then tell the coordinator / dedicated **dev server** agent: "need server restart — prisma generate then pnpm dev on :3000"
3. They do NOT generate, do NOT copy tmp clients, do NOT restart

## Restart in place (owner only)

Before starting: check if something already listens on 3000. If it is this app and healthy, leave it. If a zombie holds 3000, kill only that next/node process, then start once on 3000. Never start a second port.

```text
# BAD — any non-owner agent starts or kills the server
pnpm dev
pnpm dev --port 3001
taskkill /PID <3000> /F

# GOOD — non-owner
# Ask the coordinator / dedicated dev-server agent: "restart please"

# GOOD — owner only
# 1. Check listeners on 3000
# 2. Reuse if this app is already Ready
# 3. Or kill that next/node only, then `pnpm dev` once on 3000
```

```text
# BAD — any non-owner generates or copies over a locked Prisma engine
npx prisma generate
npx prisma generate --generator client --output prisma-tmp
# then copy prisma-tmp over generated/prisma
# bump lib/db.ts singleton key so the old client is ignored

# GOOD — non-owner
# MAY: npx prisma migrate deploy (if safe)
# Then ask the coordinator / dedicated dev-server agent:
# "need server restart — prisma generate then pnpm dev on :3000"

# GOOD — owner only
# Stop :3000 if needed, prisma generate, then pnpm dev once on 3000
```
